            <td>90.1%</td>
            <td>82.3%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Pathology</td>
            <td>84.0%</td>
            <td>74.1%</td>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="box">
        <h2>Safety, Bias, and Health Equity</h2>
        <p>Despite encouraging accuracy figures, safety and equity concerns persist. Disparities in model performance exist, yet assessment remains rare.</p>

        <div class="stat-huge" style="color: var(--accent1);">18%</div>
        <div class="stat-label">of published studies reported any formal assessment of algorithmic bias across demographic groups</div>

        <div id="chart-safety" class="chart-container" style="height: 300px;"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Right Column -->
    <div class="col">
      <div class="box box-highlight">
        <h2>The Translational Implementation Gap</h2>
        <p>While the FDA had cleared 692 AI/ML-enabled medical devices by 2023, the vast majority of AI models never reach real-world validation.</p>

        <div class="stat-huge" style="color: var(--accent2);">&lt; 5%</div>
        <div class="stat-label" style="color: white;">Prospective Validation Rate of Published AI Models</div>

        <div id="chart-gap" class="chart-container-large"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="box">
        <h2>Recommendations & Future Directions</h2>
        <p>Closing the gap between AI research promise and clinical reality requires coordinated action:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Mandate prospective validation</b> before clinical deployment, including multi-site and diverse-population trials.</li>
